module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.PowerTransitionColimit

/-!
# The union is the colimit of its degrees: the chain form

Let `S` be a scheme, `𝒜` a graded `𝒪_S`-algebra (Situation 01NN) and `T` a test scheme. The set
`F(T)` of the display 01NX is the set of quadruples of positive degree modulo the equivalence
relation **generated** by two identifications: strict equivalence inside a degree, and the
equivalence of Tag 01NW across degrees. Two quadruples therefore have the same point of `F(T)`
exactly when some *chain* of those identifications joins them, and a chain may pass through
arbitrarily many intermediate degrees.

`...PowerTransitionColimit.Fd.scale_eq_of_equivalent` collapses a **single** step of such a
chain: two equivalent quadruples of degrees `d` and `d'` already have the same class in
`F_{d d'}(T)` after the transitions. This file collapses a chain of arbitrary length, which is
the statement that `F(T)` *is* the colimit of the `F_d(T)` along the transitions rather than
merely a set receiving compatible maps from them:

> `F.mk f hd P = F.mk f hd' Q` **if and only if** there is a common multiple `e` of `d` and `d'`
> in which the transitions of `P` and of `Q` have the same class in `F_e(T)`.

## The two halves

The "if" half is `...Fd.toF_scale` — the canonical maps `F_d(T) → F(T)` identify a class with
its transition — together with `Fd.toF_congrDegree`, which says that rereading a degree at
another spelling of the same integer does not move a point of `F(T)`.

The "only if" half is an induction over the chain. The relation `CofinallyEqual` of *becoming
equal in a common degree* is shown to be an equivalence relation containing both identifications
of the union; since `F(T)` is a quotient by the equivalence relation generated by them
(`Quot.eq` and `Relation.EqvGen`), it is implied by having the same point of `F(T)`.

## Why this is bookkeeping and not new mathematics

Everything the induction needs is composition of transitions, and that is already a corollary of
Tag 01NW's machinery: `Quadruple.compatibleAt_scale` makes a quadruple compatible at `(a, 1)`
with its transition, `CompatibleAt.mul_left` restricts that compatibility to `(b a, b)`, and
`...Quadruple.strictlyEquivalent_scale_of_compatibleAt` then reads off that `P` transitioned by
`b a` is the transition by `b` of its transition by `a` — `strictlyEquivalent_scale_scale`
below. No new comparison of tensor powers is constructed anywhere in this file.

The degrees `b (a d)` and `(b a) d` are equal integers written two ways, so the statements carry
the transport `...Quadruple.congrDegree` of a quadruple across a respelling of its degree; the
lemmas collecting those transports are the bulk of the file.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.CofinallyEqual`: two quadruples of positive
  degree **become equal in a common multiple of their degrees** after the transitions.

## Main results

* `...RelativeProjQcohSheaf.Quadruple.strictlyEquivalent_scale_scale` and
  `...strictlyEquivalent_scale_scale'`: **two transitions compose to one.**
* `...RelativeProjQcohSheaf.cofinallyEqual_equivalence` and `...unionRel_le_cofinallyEqual`:
  becoming equal in a common degree is an equivalence relation, and it contains both
  identifications made by the union of the display 01NX.
* `...RelativeProjQcohSheaf.F.mk_eq_mk_iff_exists_common_degree`: **two quadruples of positive
  degree have the same point of `F(T)` if and only if their transitions into some common
  multiple of their degrees have the same class there.**

## What is not here

Representability is not proved and nothing is assumed: there is no scheme anywhere below. The
remaining steps of Tag 01NY are recorded on `...Fd.scale_eq_of_equivalent`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Section 01NS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory

open AlgebraicGeometry Stacks.RingedSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf

variable {T S : Scheme.{u}} {f : T ⟶ S}
  {A : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} (structureRingSheaf S.toRingedSpace)}

namespace Quadruple

variable {d : ℤ}

/-- **Rereading a degree at the same spelling changes nothing.** -/
theorem strictlyEquivalent_congrDegree_self (P : Quadruple f A d) (h : d = d) :
    StrictlyEquivalent (P.congrDegree h) P :=
  (strictlyEquivalent_iff_exists_hom _ _).mpr ⟨Iso.refl _, fun n => by simp⟩

/-- **Rereading a degree twice is rereading it once.** -/
theorem strictlyEquivalent_congrDegree_congrDegree (P : Quadruple f A d) {e e' : ℤ}
    (h : d = e) (h' : e = e') :
    StrictlyEquivalent ((P.congrDegree h).congrDegree h') (P.congrDegree (h.trans h')) := by
  subst h
  subst h'
  exact (strictlyEquivalent_iff_exists_hom _ _).mpr ⟨Iso.refl _, fun n => by simp⟩

/-- **The transition commutes with rereading the degree.** -/
theorem strictlyEquivalent_scale_congrDegree (P : Quadruple f A d) {a : ℤ} (ha : 0 < a)
    {e : ℤ} (h : d = e) :
    StrictlyEquivalent ((P.congrDegree h).scale ha)
      ((P.scale ha).congrDegree (congrArg (fun k => a * k) h)) := by
  subst h
  exact (strictlyEquivalent_iff_exists_hom _ _).mpr
    ⟨Iso.refl _, fun n => by simp [Twisting.scaleApp]⟩

/-- **Two transitions compose to one.** -/
theorem strictlyEquivalent_scale_scale (P : Quadruple f A d) {a b : ℤ} (ha : 0 < a)
    (hb : 0 < b) :
    StrictlyEquivalent (P.scale (mul_pos hb ha))
      (((P.scale ha).scale hb).congrDegree (show b * (a * d) = b * a * d by ring)) := by
  have h := (P.compatibleAt_scale ha).mul_left b
  rw [mul_one] at h
  exact strictlyEquivalent_scale_of_compatibleAt (mul_pos hb ha) hb h _

/-- **Two transitions compose to one**, with the common degree prescribed. -/
theorem strictlyEquivalent_scale_scale' (P : Quadruple f A d) {a b e : ℤ} (ha : 0 < a)
    (hb : 0 < b) (h : b * a * d = e) :
    StrictlyEquivalent
      (((P.scale ha).scale hb).congrDegree (show b * (a * d) = e by rw [← h]; ring))
      ((P.scale (mul_pos hb ha)).congrDegree h) :=
  strictlyEquivalent_equivalence.trans
    (strictlyEquivalent_equivalence.symm
      (strictlyEquivalent_congrDegree_congrDegree ((P.scale ha).scale hb) _ h))
    (strictlyEquivalent_equivalence.symm
      ((P.strictlyEquivalent_scale_scale ha hb).congrDegree h))

end Quadruple

/-! ### Rereading and composing the transitions on the classes -/

/-- Rereading a degree at the same spelling is the identity of `F_d(T)`. -/
@[simp] theorem Fd.congrDegree_self {d : ℤ} (h : d = d) (ξ : Fd A d T) :
    Fd.congrDegree h ξ = ξ := by
  obtain ⟨g, x⟩ := ξ
  induction x using Quotient.ind with
  | _ P => exact (Fd.mk_eq_mk_iff _ _).mpr (P.strictlyEquivalent_congrDegree_self h)

/-- **Rereading the degree is absorbed by the transition out of it.** -/
theorem Fd.congrDegree_scale_congrDegree {d e e' a : ℤ} (ha : 0 < a) (h : d = e)
    (h2 : a * e = e') (ξ : Fd A d T) :
    Fd.congrDegree h2 (Fd.scale ha (Fd.congrDegree h ξ)) =
      Fd.congrDegree (show a * d = e' by rw [h]; exact h2) (Fd.scale ha ξ) := by
  subst h
  rw [Fd.congrDegree_self]

/-- **Two transitions compose to one**, on the classes, with the common degree prescribed. -/
theorem Fd.congrDegree_scale_scale {d a b e : ℤ} (ha : 0 < a) (hb : 0 < b)
    (h : b * a * d = e) (ξ : Fd A d T) :
    Fd.congrDegree (show b * (a * d) = e by rw [← h]; ring) (Fd.scale hb (Fd.scale ha ξ)) =
      Fd.congrDegree h (Fd.scale (mul_pos hb ha) ξ) := by
  obtain ⟨g, x⟩ := ξ
  induction x using Quotient.ind with
  | _ P => exact (Fd.mk_eq_mk_iff _ _).mpr (P.strictlyEquivalent_scale_scale' ha hb h)

/-- **Rereading the degree does not change the point of `F(T)`.** -/
theorem Fd.toF_congrDegree {d e : ℤ} (hd : 0 < d) (he : 0 < e) (h : d = e) (ξ : Fd A d T) :
    Fd.toF he (Fd.congrDegree h ξ) = Fd.toF hd ξ := by
  subst h
  rw [Fd.congrDegree_self]

/-- **Two transitions out of a reread degree compose to one**, with the final degree
prescribed. -/
theorem Fd.congrDegree_scale_congrDegree_scale {d e e' a b : ℤ} (ha : 0 < a) (hb : 0 < b)
    (h : a * d = e) (h2 : b * e = e') (ξ : Fd A d T) :
    Fd.congrDegree h2 (Fd.scale hb (Fd.congrDegree h (Fd.scale ha ξ))) =
      Fd.congrDegree (show b * a * d = e' by rw [← h2, ← h]; ring)
        (Fd.scale (mul_pos hb ha) ξ) := by
  rw [Fd.congrDegree_scale_congrDegree hb h h2,
    Fd.congrDegree_scale_scale ha hb (show b * a * d = e' by rw [← h2, ← h]; ring)]

/-- **Applying one more transition to an equality of classes in a common degree** composes the
transitions on both sides. -/
private theorem Fd.congrDegree_scale_eq_of_eq {d d' e E a a' b : ℤ} (ha : 0 < a) (ha' : 0 < a')
    (hb : 0 < b) (h : a * d = e) (h' : a' * d' = e) (hE : b * e = E) {ξ : Fd A d T}
    {ξ' : Fd A d' T}
    (hξ : Fd.congrDegree h (Fd.scale ha ξ) = Fd.congrDegree h' (Fd.scale ha' ξ')) :
    Fd.congrDegree (show b * a * d = E by rw [← hE, ← h]; ring) (Fd.scale (mul_pos hb ha) ξ) =
      Fd.congrDegree (show b * a' * d' = E by rw [← hE, ← h']; ring)
        (Fd.scale (mul_pos hb ha') ξ') := by
  have := congrArg (fun ζ => Fd.congrDegree hE (Fd.scale hb ζ)) hξ
  simpa only [Fd.congrDegree_scale_congrDegree_scale ha hb h hE,
    Fd.congrDegree_scale_congrDegree_scale ha' hb h' hE] using this

/-- **The transition into a prescribed degree does not depend on the spelling of its factor.** -/
theorem Fd.congrDegree_scale_congr {d e a a' : ℤ} (ha : 0 < a) (ha' : 0 < a') (haa : a = a')
    (h : a * d = e) (h' : a' * d = e) (ξ : Fd A d T) :
    Fd.congrDegree h (Fd.scale ha ξ) = Fd.congrDegree h' (Fd.scale ha' ξ) := by
  subst haa
  rfl

/-! ### Becoming equal in a common degree -/

/-- **The identification that the colimit of the transitions makes.** Two quadruples of positive
degree over `f : T ⟶ S` are *cofinally equal* when, after the transitions
`F_d(T) → F_e(T)` into some common multiple `e` of their degrees, their classes are already
equal in `F_e(T)`. -/
def CofinallyEqual (x y : PositiveQuadruple f A) : Prop :=
  ∃ (e a a' : ℤ) (ha : 0 < a) (ha' : 0 < a') (h : a * x.1.1 = e) (h' : a' * y.1.1 = e),
    Fd.congrDegree h (Fd.scale ha (Fd.mk f x.2)) =
      Fd.congrDegree h' (Fd.scale ha' (Fd.mk f y.2))

/-- **Cofinal equality is an equivalence relation.** Transitivity is the only content: a common
degree for `x, y` and one for `y, z` are carried into a single one by two further transitions,
which compose by `Fd.congrDegree_scale_congrDegree_scale`. -/
theorem cofinallyEqual_equivalence : Equivalence (CofinallyEqual (f := f) (A := A)) where
  refl x := ⟨1 * x.1.1, 1, 1, one_pos, one_pos, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩
  symm := fun ⟨e, a, a', ha, ha', h, h', hEq⟩ => ⟨e, a', a, ha', ha, h', h, hEq.symm⟩
  trans := by
    rintro x y z ⟨e₁, a, a', ha, ha', h, h', eq₁⟩ ⟨e₂, b, b', hb, hb', k, k', eq₂⟩
    have hE : a' * e₂ = b * e₁ := by rw [← k, ← h']; ring
    refine ⟨b * e₁, b * a, a' * b', mul_pos hb ha, mul_pos ha' hb',
      by rw [← h]; ring, by rw [← hE, ← k']; ring, ?_⟩
    exact (Fd.congrDegree_scale_eq_of_eq ha ha' hb h h' rfl eq₁).trans (Eq.trans
      (Fd.congrDegree_scale_congr (mul_pos hb ha') (mul_pos ha' hb) (mul_comm b a') _ _ _)
      (Fd.congrDegree_scale_eq_of_eq hb hb' ha' k k' hE eq₂))

/-- **Both identifications the union of the display 01NX makes are cofinal equalities.** For
strictly equivalent quadruples of one degree there is nothing to do; for equivalent quadruples
of degrees `d` and `d'` this is `Fd.scale_eq_of_equivalent`, the common degree being `d' d`. -/
theorem unionRel_le_cofinallyEqual :
    UnionRel (f := f) (A := A) ≤ CofinallyEqual := by
  intro x y hxy
  induction hxy with
  | @strict c P Q h =>
      exact ⟨1 * c.1, 1, 1, one_pos, one_pos, rfl, rfl, by rw [(Fd.mk_eq_mk_iff P Q).mpr h]⟩
  | @equivalent c c' P Q h =>
      refine ⟨c'.1 * c.1, c'.1, c.1, c'.2, c.2, rfl, mul_comm c.1 c'.1, ?_⟩
      rw [Fd.congrDegree_self]
      exact Fd.scale_eq_of_equivalent c.2 c'.2 h

/-! ### The colimit statement -/

/-- **The union of the display 01NX is the colimit of its degrees along the transitions.** Two
quadruples of positive degrees `d` and `d'` over the same morphism `f : T ⟶ S` have the same
point of `F(T)` *exactly* when there is a common multiple `e` of `d` and `d'` in which their
transitions `F_d(T) → F_e(T)` and `F_{d'}(T) → F_e(T)` already have the same class.

One direction says the transitions are collapsed by the union (`Fd.toF_scale`); the other says
nothing else is, and it is an induction over a chain of identifications of arbitrary length,
`F(T)` being a quotient by the equivalence relation they generate. Together with
`F.exists_quadruple`, which says every point of `F(T)` comes from some `F_d(T)`, this is the
colimit property of `F(T)` at a single test scheme. -/
-- Beyond what this declaration proves, recorded here rather than in the attribute:
--   the representability of F is NOT proved here and nothing is assumed: the union F(T) of the
--   display 01NX IS the colimit of the F_d(T) along the transitions, in the chain form two
--   quadruples of positive degrees d and d' have the same point of F(T) if and only if their
--   transitions into some common multiple e of d and d' already have the same class in F_e(T). The
--   forward direction is an induction over a chain of identifications of arbitrary length (F(T) is
--   a quotient by the equivalence relation generated by strict equivalence and Tag 01NW's
--   equivalence), which is what `Fd.scale_eq_of_equivalent` a single step does not give. This
--   closes residue (iv) recorded on that declaration. NOTHING IS MISSING for Tag 01NY any more:
--   residue (i), the representability of each F_d by a scheme U_d over S, is Tag 01NU proved over
--   an affine base as AffineFdRepresentable.Fd.representableByDegreeOpen and descended to a
--   general base as ChartDegreeOpenEquiv.ProjDegreeRepresentation.ofCharts and residue (iii), the
--   nesting and covering of the U_d, is RelativeProjData.isOpenCover_degreeOpen; the tag itself is
--   RelativeProjRepresents.F.representableByRelativeProjOfCharts, unconditional over an arbitrary
--   base
theorem F.mk_eq_mk_iff_exists_common_degree {d d' : ℤ} (hd : 0 < d) (hd' : 0 < d')
    (P : Quadruple f A d) (Q : Quadruple f A d') :
    F.mk f hd P = F.mk f hd' Q ↔
      ∃ (e a a' : ℤ) (ha : 0 < a) (ha' : 0 < a') (h : a * d = e) (h' : a' * d' = e),
        Fd.congrDegree h (Fd.scale ha (Fd.mk f P)) =
          Fd.congrDegree h' (Fd.scale ha' (Fd.mk f Q)) := by
  refine ⟨fun hPQ => ?_, fun ⟨e, a, a', ha, ha', h, h', hEq⟩ => ?_⟩
  · have h2 : Quot.mk (UnionRel (f := f) (A := A)) ⟨⟨d, hd⟩, P⟩ =
        Quot.mk _ ⟨⟨d', hd'⟩, Q⟩ := eq_of_heq (Sigma.mk.injEq .. ▸ hPQ).2
    exact cofinallyEqual_equivalence.eqvGen_iff.mp
      (Relation.EqvGen.mono unionRel_le_cofinallyEqual _ _ (Quot.eq.mp h2))
  · have he : 0 < e := h ▸ mul_pos ha hd
    have hc := congrArg (Fd.toF he) hEq
    rw [Fd.toF_congrDegree (mul_pos ha hd) he h, Fd.toF_congrDegree (mul_pos ha' hd') he h',
      Fd.toF_scale hd ha, Fd.toF_scale hd' ha', Fd.toF_mk, Fd.toF_mk] at hc
    exact hc

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf

end
